# The Moon's Eternal Dance

Long ago, when the world was young, the Moon shone as bright as the Sun. She was vain and boastful, declaring herself the most beautiful light in the heavens. The Sun, generous and wise, said nothing, but the Stars grew tired of Moon's arrogance.

"If you are so magnificent," challenged the eldest Star, "then share your light equally with all creatures, every night, without rest."

Moon laughed. "I shall outshine you all, forever!"

