Terrified, Moon begged forgiveness. The Stars took pity and agreed to restore her, but only gradually. "You will learn humility," they said. "Each month, you will fade and return, remembering that even the brightest light needs rest and renewal."

And so Moon waxes and wanes, growing from a silver crescent to fullness, then fading again to shadow. In her cycle, she teaches us that all things must balance pride with humility, light with darkness, fullness with emptiness.
